### Non-text file via the S3 API directly (bypasses Artel entirely — talks straight to the
### Garage/S3-compatible bucket linked to the vault, path-style per client.go's
### BucketLookupPath requirement for Garage). Unlike CouchDB's Basic auth, S3 requires
### AWS SigV4 request signing, which the IntelliJ HTTP Client cannot generate natively.
### These requests are not runnable as-is from this file — sign them with an external
### client (aws-cli, mc, Postman) using {{s3_access_key}}/{{s3_secret_key}}. They document
### the wire-level request shape (method/path/headers) that Artel's minio-go client sends.
### test.png in ../test.png is an empty file, used here as request body.

### Upload binary file (test.png, saved under the "s3" folder)
PUT {{garage_s3_url}}/{{s3_bucket}}/s3/test.png
Content-Type: image/png
Authorization: AWS4-HMAC-SHA256 Credential={{s3_access_key}}/..., SignedHeaders=host;x-amz-content-sha256;x-amz-date, Signature=...

< ../test.png

### List objects in bucket (verify s3/test.png appears)
GET {{garage_s3_url}}/{{s3_bucket}}?list-type=2
Authorization: AWS4-HMAC-SHA256 Credential={{s3_access_key}}/..., SignedHeaders=host;x-amz-content-sha256;x-amz-date, Signature=...

### Read binary file back
GET {{garage_s3_url}}/{{s3_bucket}}/s3/test.png
Authorization: AWS4-HMAC-SHA256 Credential={{s3_access_key}}/..., SignedHeaders=host;x-amz-content-sha256;x-amz-date, Signature=...

### Get object metadata (HEAD)
HEAD {{garage_s3_url}}/{{s3_bucket}}/s3/test.png
Authorization: AWS4-HMAC-SHA256 Credential={{s3_access_key}}/..., SignedHeaders=host;x-amz-content-sha256;x-amz-date, Signature=...

### Delete binary file
DELETE {{garage_s3_url}}/{{s3_bucket}}/s3/test.png
Authorization: AWS4-HMAC-SHA256 Credential={{s3_access_key}}/..., SignedHeaders=host;x-amz-content-sha256;x-amz-date, Signature=...